# ACCEPTED RISK: nltk 3.9.2 (transitive dependency of textblob 0.19.0)
#
# CVE-2025-14009, CVE-2026-78683, CVE-2026-79657, CVE-2026-79675, and related path-traversal /
# file-read / pickle-deserialization / ReDoS CVEs in nltk's corpus loaders, downloader and Java wrappers.
#
# Why not fixed: every patched nltk release (3.9.3+ and 3.10.x) requires Python >= 3.10.
# This image uses Python 3.9, so pip cannot install a fixed version.
#
# Why the risk is low (verified in code): the app never imports nltk directly. The only use is
# home/views.py: TextBlob(feedback_text).sentiment.polarity, which scores a plain string.
# It never calls nltk.download(), never loads pickled nltk models/tokenizers, never parses nltk
# corpora or XML, and never uses the Java wrappers, so none of the vulnerable code paths run.
#
# Mitigation and follow-up: upgrade the base image to Python 3.12, then bump nltk.
CVE-2025-14009
CVE-2026-0846
CVE-2026-0847
CVE-2026-12061
CVE-2026-12072
CVE-2026-12074
CVE-2026-12075
